course: dictionary
lesson: 3165
title: Emotion: strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An emotion is a strong feeling inside you. Happiness, sadness, fear, anger, love and surprise are all emotions. Everyone has them, and every emotion is normal.
explain: The word can also describe how strongly someone feels when they speak or act. «She read the poem with emotion» means her voice showed strong feeling. Look at the words around emotion to see which meaning fits.
explain: Stories show emotions too. A character's face, voice and actions can tell you how they feel, even when the author never uses the word. Understanding feelings, in yourself and in others, is called emotional literacy.
fact: An emotion is a strong feeling, such as happiness, sadness, fear, anger, love or surprise.
fact: Emotion can also mean strong feeling in general, as in «speaks with emotion».
fact: Useful phrases: «show emotion», «mixed emotions», «hide your emotions», «full of emotion».
fact: All emotions are normal, and learning safe ways to handle anger or worry is important.
fact: Science today shows that many animals feel pain and emotions.
exercise: Which of these is an emotion? | Blue | *Fear | Table | Running
exercise: «She spoke with emotion, and her voice shook.» What does emotion mean here? | Something she had for lunch | A small, quiet noise | A list of facts | *Strong feeling showing in her voice
exercise: «Jamal's face showed fear when the lights went out.» Find and copy one emotion word. | face | *fear | out | lights
test: «The crowd was full of emotion as the team won.» What does full of emotion suggest? | Empty seats | *Strong feelings showing | Quiet and calm | Lost in a maze
test: Which of these is NOT an emotion? | Anger | Love | Surprise | *Table
exam: Which phrase means someone is hiding how they feel? | *Hide your emotions | Mixed emotions | Full of emotion | Show emotion
